{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they assembled against Moses and against Aaron.</b> Korah, Dathan, and Abiram assembled to lodge their complaint against Moses and Aaron in the presence of the two hundred and fifty princes of the congregation, who had gone there at the counsel of these complainers at the time when men of the children of Israel would come before Moses for judgment. And those two hundred and fifty gathered there as though going innocently to Moses to stand with him there, so that when Korah, Dathan, and Abiram afterward assembled against Moses and Aaron, they would all be as one, concurring with the words of the assembled before those men of the children of Israel who were present there. And they chose an hour when a multitude of people would be there, in order to publicize and spread the word throughout the camp, so that many would rise up with them." "<b>For all the congregation.</b> Each one of them." "<b>They are all holy.</b> From the sole of the foot to the head, as it says: וִהְיִיתֶם קְדוֹשִׁים לֵאלֹהֵיכֶם (Numbers 15:40)." "<b>And why do you lift yourselves up.</b> In the matter of holiness — that you restricted the service to the firstborn, when Moses had already officiated for all seven days of consecration, and Aaron and his sons are priests forever."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:04.521876473Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}